---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Yeh Bro is an Australia-first bodybuilding and lifting brand — evidence-first education, legal sports nutrition, and PED harm-reduction without selling gear."
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>Serious lifting. Honest industry talk.</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Yeh Bro is an Australia-first bodybuilding and lifting brand: evidence, AUD reality, and culture
			literacy — not overnight-gain reels or mystery blends.
		</p>

		<h2>Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			We publish guides for people who train hard and want straight answers — creatine, protein, pre,
			and the rest of legal sports nutrition — plus clear talk about how the industry actually works.
			Bodybuilding culture includes PED use for some athletes. Ignoring that helps nobody. Pretending
			powder is “like gear but natural” helps nobody either.
		</p>

		<h2>How we educate (including PEDs)</h2>
		<p>
			When we cover PED reality, the frame is <strong>harm reduction</strong>, not moral panic and not
			a shop:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Health risks and why medical care / bloodwork matter if someone chooses that path</li>
			<li>Australian legal context at a high level — not sourcing tips</li>
			<li>Separating marketing fairytales from what training and food actually do</li>
			<li>Support supplements stay in the legal sports-nutrition / general-wellness lane</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We are not a clinic. Nothing here is medical advice, diagnosis, or a green light to break the
			law.
		</p>

		<h2>How we pick products we link</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Evidence and clear labels over marketing copy</li>
			<li>Dose you can verify — proprietary blends are a red flag</li>
			<li>AU availability and price per effective dose</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Affiliate / product recommendations:</strong> legal sports nutrition only (creatine,
				protein, pre/intra, basics) — never “on-cycle stack” shop framing that implies unlawful
				supply
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We are not pay-to-rank. Sponsored posts, if any, get labelled separately.</p>

		<h2>What we never do</h2>
		<div class="skip-flag">
			<p>
				We do <strong>not</strong> sell, source, or promote buying illegal AAS, restricted SARMs,
				unapproved peptides, underground lab gear, or grey-market “buy gear” / cycle-blast-PCT product
				funnels. Comment bait asking for sources gets refused. Education ≠ a storefront.
			</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>
		<p>
			Some links use <code>/go/</code> redirects. If you buy, we may earn a commission at no extra
			cost to you. Full policy on <a href="/disclosure">Disclosure</a>.
		</p>

		<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/start-here">Start here</a></p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
